{"name":"Reed Bed","hex":"#b0ad96","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"reed bed","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A place where reeds grow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/reed_bed"}],"entries":[{"title":"Reed bed","blocks":[{"text":"A reedbed or reed bed is a natural habitat found in floodplains, waterlogged depressions and \nestuaries. Reedbeds are part of a succession from young reeds colonising open water or wet ground through a gradation of increasingly dry ground. As reedbeds age, they build up a considerable litter layer that eventually rises above the water level and that ultimately provides opportunities in the form of new areas for larger terrestrial plants such as shrubs and trees to colonise."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Phragmites_australis1.jpg/330px-Phragmites_australis1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_bed","wikidata":"Q620424"},{"title":"Reed (plant)","blocks":[{"text":"Reed is the common name for several tall, grass-like plants found in wetlands."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Reeds%2C_Reeds%2C_Reeds._-_geograph.org.uk_-_366871.jpg/330px-Reeds%2C_Reeds%2C_Reeds._-_geograph.org.uk_-_366871.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_(plant)","wikidata":"Q2734060"},{"title":"Bed","blocks":[{"text":"A bed is a piece of furniture that is used as a place to sleep, rest, and relax."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg/330px-2008-04-12_Freilichtmuseum_Detmold_%2811%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bed","wikidata":"Q42177"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Harchies_%28Belgique